---
/**
 * EN — Pillar (W293): Solar panel prices in Morocco. Faithful translation of
 * /prix-panneaux-solaires-maroc — evergreen, every figure mirrors the FR 1:1
 * (same source: the dated blog post prix-installation-solaire-maroc-2026).
 * Internal links use localizeNavHref (EN/AR if available, else the existing
 * FR page — never a dead link). FR untouched.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pageLocale } from '../../lib/pageCtx';
import V2Enhance from '../../components/V2Enhance.astro';
import Article33Ribbon from '../../components/Article33Ribbon.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import CtaLigne from '../../components/CtaLigne.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import StickyCta from '../../components/StickyCta.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import { NAP } from '../../lib/nap';
import { localizeNavHref } from '../../i18n/pages';
import { PHRASE_TVA } from '../../lib/prixConstants';

const { locale, L } = pageLocale(Astro.url.pathname);

const verifiedDate = new Date('2026-11-04');
const dateFmt = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });

// WAUD68 (D-WAUD-5 = a) — no amount until lib/prixConstants.ts has its dated source (removed figures
// listed there).
const faq = [
  {
    q: 'How much does a turnkey solar installation cost in Morocco?',
    a: 'The price depends on the power chosen from your bill, the roof, any battery and the brands installed. We do not publish a bracket without a dated source: the price of your installation comes from a free study of your bill.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why should a very low price per kWc be a warning sign?',
    a: 'It often matches the equipment kit alone (panels + inverter), without installation, wiring, structure or connection — not a finished turnkey installation. Always compare two offers line by line.',
  },
  {

    q: 'What is the return on investment for a solar installation in Morocco?',
    a: 'The calculation depends heavily on your actual consumption and your ONEE tariff bracket.',
  },
];

const url = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site).href;
const schemaImageUrl = new URL('/og/residentiel.png', Astro.site).href;
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Solar panel prices in Morocco: what makes the price',
  description: 'What makes the price of a turnkey solar installation in Morocco: power (kWc), roof, battery, brands — and why the real figure comes from your bill.',
  image: schemaImageUrl,
  dateModified: verifiedDate.toISOString().slice(0, 10),
  about: { '@type': 'Thing', name: 'Solar installation price Morocco' },
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: NAP.name, url: NAP.url },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: NAP.name, url: NAP.url },
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
};
---

<Layout
  title="Solar panel prices in Morocco: what makes the price | Taqinor"
  description="How much does a solar installation cost in Morocco? What makes the price: power (kWc), roof, battery, brands, VAT — and why the real figure comes from your bill."
  ogSlug="residentiel"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  <div class="v2">
    <V2Enhance />
    <Article33Ribbon />

    <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: L('/') }, { label: 'Solar panel prices in Morocco' }]} />

    <article class="mx-auto max-w-[68ch] px-4 pb-24 pt-12 sm:pb-28">
      <p class="tech-label v2-kicker rule-brass text-lune">Prices &amp; quotes</p>
      <h1 class="display v2-page-title mt-5 text-white">Solar panel prices in Morocco</h1>

      <p class="guide-byline mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-xs text-lune-faint">
        <span>Page reviewed {dateFmt.format(verifiedDate)} · by Reda Kasri</span>
      </p>

      <p class="v2-lead mt-6 text-lune-soft">
        "How much does it really cost?" is the first question in almost every one of our meetings.
        This page explains what makes the price of an installation and how to read an offer —
        without copying a bracket whose dated source we cannot show. The price of YOUR installation
        comes from a free study of your bill.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display v2-section-title mt-12 text-white">What a turnkey price covers</h2>
      <p class="v2-lead mt-5 text-lune-soft">
        A turnkey price covers the supply of the equipment <strong class="text-white">and</strong> the
        complete installation: panels, inverter, structure, wiring, AC/DC protection, commissioning
        and, depending on the power, the Law 82-21 declaration. The total depends first on the
        <strong class="text-white">power (kWc)</strong> chosen from your consumption, then on the roof
        type, the distance to the electrical panel, the brands installed and any battery. An on-site
        quote remains essential.
      </p>
      <CtaLigne />

      <h2 class="display v2-section-title mt-12 text-white">Beware of a very low price per kWc</h2>
      <p class="v2-lead mt-5 text-lune-soft">
        A price per kWc that looks unbeatable often matches the <strong class="text-white">equipment
        kit alone</strong> (panels + inverter, without installation, wiring, structure or
        connection) — not a finished installation. Compare two offers line by line, item by item.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display v2-section-title mt-12 text-white">The roof moves the price</h2>
      <p class="v2-lead mt-5 text-lune-soft">
        An easily accessible concrete terrace remains the least expensive configuration. A tile or
        corrugated-sheet roof calls for a more technical installation, and a steep slope (above 30°)
        for safety equipment: these extra costs appear on the installation line of your quote.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display v2-section-title mt-12 text-white">The battery question: useful, but not cost-neutral</h2>
      <p class="v2-lead mt-5 text-lune-soft">
        An installation <strong class="text-white">without a battery</strong> (grid-tied) remains the
        most common solution for most urban homes. An LFP battery, to store energy for the evening or
        ride through outages, adds a major item to the quote and lengthens the payback time: it is
        only justified by your consumption profile.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display v2-section-title mt-12 text-white">VAT</h2>
      <p class="v2-lead mt-5 text-lune-soft">{PHRASE_TVA.en}</p>

      <h2 class="display v2-section-title mt-12 text-white">Return on investment</h2>
      <p class="v2-lead mt-5 text-lune-soft">
        This calculation depends heavily on your actual consumption
        and your ONEE tariff bracket — see our
        <a href={L('/financement')} class="border-b border-azur-200/60 pb-0.5 font-semibold text-azur-200 transition-colors hover:text-white">financing & returns</a>
        page for detail, and the article
        <a href={L('/blog/rentabilite-solaire-par-ville-maroc')} class="border-b border-azur-200/60 pb-0.5 font-semibold text-azur-200 transition-colors hover:text-white">profitability by city</a>
        for regional figures.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display v2-section-title mt-12 text-white">How many panels do you need?</h2>
      <p class="v2-lead mt-5 text-lune-soft">
        Before comparing prices, you need to know the right power for your household. A household
        consuming between 4,000 and 6,000 kWh/year generally needs 3 to 5 kWc; between 6,000 and
        10,000 kWh/year, more like 5 to 8 kWc. Our dedicated guide covers the full method:
        <a href={L('/guides/combien-de-panneaux-pour-ma-maison')} class="border-b border-azur-200/60 pb-0.5 font-semibold text-azur-200 transition-colors hover:text-white">how many panels for my house?</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="display v2-section-title mt-12 text-white">A last word before signing anything</h2>
      <p class="v2-lead mt-5 text-lune-soft">
        No public bracket gives a firm price. Your roof configuration, your consumption, your ONEE
        bracket and the distance between the panels and the electrical panel move the final total.
        The only figure that counts for your house comes from reading your bill and a visit — free
        and with no obligation.
      </p>
      <p class="v2-lead mt-3 text-xs text-lune-faint">
        For what makes up the bill in 2026 (equipment, labour, paperwork), see our article
        <a href={L('/blog/prix-installation-solaire-maroc-2026')} class="border-b border-white/40 pb-0.5 font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:border-white">How much does a solar installation cost in Morocco in 2026?</a>
      </p>

      <RelatedLinks links={[
        { href: L('/résidentiel'), label: 'Our residential solutions' },
        { href: L('/nos-solutions'), label: 'All our solutions' },
        { href: L('/guides'), label: 'All the guides' },
        { href: L('/blog'), label: 'The blog' },
      ]} />
    </article>

    <!-- W297 — visual FAQ: schema={false}, /faq keeps the site's only FAQPage -->
    <Faq items={faq} heading="Solar panel prices — frequently asked questions" schema={false} />

    <CtaBand title="The only figure that matters is yours. Launch the free study." href={L('/devis/mon-toit')} />

    <StickyCta />
  </div>
</Layout>
